      },
      "notes": "PK parameters of meropenem and H-4295 after [14C]meropenem 120 mg/kg IV\nS03 | DOI 10.11250/chemotherapy1953.40.Supplement1_145 | Table 1 (Iba et al. 1992, dogs and monkeys)\nBeagle dogs (male 15.2-17.5 kg, female 13.0-15.1 kg, ICI). Unlabeled meropenem (Sumitomo, Lot No. P239, purity 99%) dissolved in water for injection; [14C]meropenem (radiochemical purity >=98%) dissolved in that solution. [14C]meropenem 120 mg/kg single IV (dose volume printed \"120 mg/kg/ml\"). Plasma study: female dogs n = 3, sampling 5, 10, 20, 40 min, 1, 1.5, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 12 h; blood mixed at once with oxalate or heparin, then centrifuged.\nMeropenem by HPLC; H-4295 (open-ring metabolite) by radioimmunoassay; 1- or 2-compartment analysis. Each value mean ± SE of 3 dogs.\nText: plasma meropenem 1163 µg/ml immediately after dosing, initial half-life 5 min, terminal half-life 40 min; H-4295 36.7 µg/ml at 5 min, half-life 1.06 h. Concentration-time curves (14C, meropenem, H-4295) are in Fig. 1 only (not digitized).",
